  "description": "Like a released balloon, a rocket throws gas downward and the gas pushes it up (Newton's third law), so it works in a vacuum too. It carries its own oxidizer, and most of its liftoff weight is propellant, which is why it uses stages that drop away. To stay in orbit it needs about 28,000 km/h, and today some boosters come back and land to be reused. Original 3D animation; not to scale.",
